%% Source for images/how-a-file-moves.svg
%% Facts this diagram is allowed to say:
%% 1. Files start on a card, a phone, or an old drive.
%% 2. The app runs on the user's laptop, or on dedicated machines on the local network. One hub or several.
%% 3. That computer copies originals to a bucket in the customer's cloud account.
%% 4. The source may be erased only after the local copy and the bucket copy both exist.
%% 5. Search is on the web or the phone: newest first; caption, OCR, face, transcript; original folder path kept.
%% A phone folder that is still syncing is copied and never deleted. That rule is in the page text, not this picture.
flowchart TD
  shoot["1. You shoot"] --> local["2. Your laptop, or a local hub. One or several."]
  local --> bucket["3. It copies them into your cloud bucket"]
  bucket --> erase["4. Then the card can be erased"]
  erase --> find["5. You search on the web or your phone"]
